Anteater Poker
Version: Beta Release
Date: May 30, 2026

//=============================================================================
Project Overview
//=============================================================================
Anteater Poker is a networked, client-server card game developed in the C programming language.
The application facilitates remote gameplay among friends, utilizing TCP/IP sockets for
communication and GTK 3.0 for the graphical user interface.

This version extends standard Texas Hold'em rules by integrating UCI's mascot through custom
Anteater face cards and special action cards.

//=============================================================================
System Requirements
//=============================================================================
This software is designed for and verified with the following configurations:
* Operating System: Linux
* Compiler: GCC (C11 standard recommended)
* Libraries: GTK 3.0
* Build Tool: GNU Make

//=============================================================================
Execution
//=============================================================================
The application now utilizes an embedded server architecture for peer-to-peer hosting.

1. Launch the Client:
* ./bin/poker_client

2. From the main menu, select "Host Private Game" to automatically spawn the background 
server and generate a Room Code, or select "Join via Room Code" to connect to an existing host.

//=============================================================================
Release History
//=============================================================================
May 30, 2026 - V2.0
Beta Release
* Re-architected GUI into a GTK 3.0 Single-Page Application (SPA) with a dynamic layout stack.
* Embedded the automated poker bots as pthreads within the authoritative server process space.
* Integrated decentralized peer-to-peer lobby routing via Hexadecimal Room Codes.
* Added advanced UI overlays: Active Round Timer and Ranked Showdown Leaderboard.
* Updated build automation for split Beta documentation (Customer vs. Source distribution).

May 25, 2026 - V1.0
Alpha Release
* Includes proper README, COPYRIGHT, INSTALL documentation
* Bundle with Poker User Manual and Software Spec
* Generic Poker Server & Client UI implementation

